From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gibranak <gibranhostel@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] events: tolerate missing MessageID in Subscribe

Some NVRs (seen with a TP-Link NVR) send Subscribe without a WS-Addressing
MessageID header. Subscribe then returned a fault *after* the subscription
had already been created, so the NVR retried every ~2s: one orphaned
subscription and an error line per retry, flooding the 64KB syslog.

Handle it the way Renew already does: generate a UUID for RelatesTo.

--- a/src/events_service.c
+++ b/src/events_service.c
@@ -697,9 +697,13 @@
 
     relates_to_uuid = get_element("MessageID", "Header");
     if (relates_to_uuid == NULL) {
-        log_error("No MessageID element for Subscribe method");
-        send_action_failed_fault("events_service", -6);
-        return -6;
+        // Be tolerant, as Renew is: some NVRs (e.g. TP-Link) omit MessageID.
+        // Failing here left the subscription already created above, and the
+        // client retried every few seconds, flooding the log and the table.
+        log_warn("Subscribe: missing MessageID; generating one for RelatesTo");
+        static char sub_rel_uuid_buf[UUID_LEN + 1];
+        gen_uuid(sub_rel_uuid_buf);
+        relates_to_uuid = sub_rel_uuid_buf;
     }
 
     to_iso_date(iso_str, sizeof(iso_str), now);
